  "notes": "GAAP city. Governmental lines from the governmental funds statement Total column (p5); business-type from the proprietary statement Total Funds column (p7). Governmental 'Taxes' 116,736 (General 65,956 + Debt Service 50,780) kept as one line, category taxes: the Statement of Activities 'Taxes - property' 112,233 does not tie. Ending cash = Cash + Cash with County Treasurer from the governmental funds balance sheet (p4); restricted cash 408,564 excluded; no beginning cash printed. Proceeds from sale of assets 16,000 in other_financing. Business 'Other' operating revenue shown as Miscellaneous general revenue on the Statement of Activities (not in charges for services), kept other. Governmental roll: 974,706 + 903,340 - 935,735 + 219,649 - 219,649 + 16,000 = 958,311 vs printed 958,310 (report rounding). Business: 887,643 + 1,390,264 - 1,344,797 = 933,110. General Fund net change printed on p5 reads (144,836) while (128,909) + (16,059) = (144,968) and beginning 457,559 to ending 312,591 = (144,968); digits possibly misread, not recorded as a discrepancy. Only supplementary schedule is a combined all-funds cash-basis budgetary comparison (p9), so per user rule detail is one line per individual fund column of the governmental funds (p5) and proprietary funds (p7) statements; proprietary detail totals add nonoperating interest to the printed operating totals. Capital outlay lines print no function: labelled Capital Outlay. Read pages 1-9 of 9"
